        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/assets/a87b00f9f7908fe62542ef7bca94277f040af97b4af24698dd648c167bcd3376.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1\\,{{field-1}}\\,x\\,{{field-2}}\\,5,\\,2\\,{{field-3}}\\,y\\,{{field-4}}\\,5}\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "A point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the rectangle if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1<x<5,\\,2<y<5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we also need to *include* the bottom edge ($y=2$).\n\nTherefore, we change the corresponding inequality symbol to non-strict, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1<x<5,\\,2\\le y<5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since *every* real value in these intervals is included, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<x<5,\\,2\\le y<5}\n$$",
